  "description": "BAGBET crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/n. Reported CIF formula moiety: C156 H198 Gd6 N12 Ni7 O66 2+,2(C2 H6 O1),4(C1 H4 O1),6(H2 O1),2(H1 O1 1-). From the CIF bond table, Gd1 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd2 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd3 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Ni1 (Ni) has 6 O neighbors; Ni2 (Ni) has 4 O neighbors; Ni3 (Ni) has 4 O neighbors; Ni4 (Ni) has 4 O neighbors; Gd1B (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd2B (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd3B (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Ni2B (Ni) has 4 O neighbors; Ni3B (Ni) has 4 O neighbors; Ni4B (Ni) has 4 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 18 pairs, 3 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.238-4.366 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 87.75-131.84°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [C156H198Gd6N12Ni7O66]2+·2EtOH·4MeOH·6H2O·2OH−. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 12 OAc (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 6 OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 2 OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)). Explicit bracketed charge: 2+.",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
